sphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":958,"end":958,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Repeat","start":976,"end":985,"description":"CKB motif 3"},{"type":"Region","start":988,"end":1086,"description":"Acidic patch"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1012,"end":1012,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1018,"end":1018,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1020,"end":1020,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Site","start":1072,"end":1073,"description":"Cleavage; by caspase-7"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1156,"end":1156,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1289,"end":1289,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts (phosphorylation-dependent) with CHEK1; regulates CLSPN function in checkpoint for DNA damage and replication (PubMed:12766152, PubMed:15707391, PubMed:16963448). Interacts with ATR and RAD9A and these interactions are slightly reduced during checkpoint activation (PubMed:12766152). Interacts with BRCA1 and this interaction increases during checkpoint activation (PubMed:15096610). Interacts with TIMELESS; the interaction is required for leading-strand replication (PubMed:17141802, PubMed:34694004, PubMed:34700328, PubMed:35585232). Associates with the MCM2-7 complex and other replisome factors (PubMed:27401717, PubMed:34694004, PubMed:34700328). Interacts (via the acidic patch) with CDC7; the interaction is required for phosphorylation of MCM proteins and CLASPIN by CDC7 (PubMed:27401717). Interacts with PCNA (PubMed:27401717). Interacts with FZR1 (PubMed:18662541)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q9HAW4-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":1275,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000373220.7"],"refseq":["NM_001190481.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001177410.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,526],[527,591,749]],"edits":[{"start":527,"end":590,"original":"ELEALKQ